For a custom glibc `printf` conversion:

| Format component | No specification | Explicit value | `*` in the **arginfo** function | `*` in the **handler** |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `info->width` | `0` | Specified width | `INT_MIN` | Actual `int` retrieved from the argument list |
| `info->prec` | `-1` | Specified precision | `INT_MIN` | Actual `int` retrieved from the argument list |

Thus, inside the `printf_arginfo_function`, test:

```c
if (info->width == INT_MIN) {
    /* Width was specified with *. */
}

if (info->prec == INT_MIN) {
    /* Precision was specified with *. */
}
```

The `*` width and precision arguments are `int` arguments; `parse_printf_format` records them as `PA_INT`.
